{"uid":"665bff593742b311","name":"test_bare_lookup_call_site_count_is_pinned","fullName":"tests.test_bare_lookup_inventory#test_bare_lookup_call_site_count_is_pinned","historyId":"0c149e541bc26babcf24a2e4299339ff","time":{"start":1792436573168,"stop":1792436574424,"duration":1256},"description":"Ratchet, matching `test_resource_inventory.py`'s `_EXPECTED_COUNTS`\n    style: today's exact distribution across the five kinds, confirmed by\n    direct reading of every one of the 24 call sites while building this\n    checker (see `docs/workspace-plan.md`'s `P2-Q` row and this module's own\n    `_REVIEWED_BARE_LOOKUPS` comments). The point isn't that this count is a\n    law -- it's that a change gets *noticed and looked at*, not silently\n    absorbed into a bigger or smaller total kind-by-kind without anyone\n    confirming it's still safe.\n\n    `admin_only` -> `gated` for `verification.create_verification_item_record`\n    reflects `P2-Q` slice 2 (#417), landed on `main` after this checker was\n    first written: its `identity is not None` branch now routes through\n    `get_visible` instead of a bare admin-gated lookup.\n\n    `role_gated_own_project` 1 -> 2 is `routes.prompts._require_prompt_release_access`\n    (alpha gap P0-1): the prompt promote/rollback gate looks up the prompt's hidden\n    target by name and immediately enforces the `release.apply` project role, the\n    same shape as `create_prompt_version`.\n\n    `admin_only` 6 -> 5 is `routes.skills.rollback_skill` (alpha gap P1-24): it was a bare\n    lookup behind the admin scope alone, which let a global admin who was not a member roll a\n    skill back in another project. It now resolves through `_visible_skill_or_404` with the\n    `resource.write.runtime` project role.\n    ","descriptionHtml":"<p>Ratchet, matching <code>test_resource_inventory.py</code>'s <code>_EXPECTED_COUNTS</code><br />\nstyle: today's exact distribution across the five kinds, confirmed by<br />\ndirect reading of every one of the 24 call sites while building this<br />\nchecker (see <code>docs/workspace-plan.md</code>'s <code>P2-Q</code> row and this module's own<br />\n<code>_REVIEWED_BARE_LOOKUPS</code> comments). The point isn't that this count is a<br />\nlaw -- it's that a change gets <em>noticed and looked at</em>, not silently<br />\nabsorbed into a bigger or smaller total kind-by-kind without anyone<br />\nconfirming it's still safe.</p>\n<pre><code>`admin_only` -&gt; `gated` for `verification.create_verification_item_record`\nreflects `P2-Q` slice 2 (#417), landed on `main` after this checker was\nfirst written: its `identity is not None` branch now routes through\n`get_visible` instead of a bare admin-gated lookup.\n\n`role_gated_own_project` 1 -&gt; 2 is `routes.prompts._require_prompt_release_access`\n(alpha gap P0-1): the prompt promote/rollback gate looks up the prompt's hidden\ntarget by name and immediately enforces the `release.apply` project role, the\nsame shape as `create_prompt_version`.\n\n`admin_only` 6 -&gt; 5 is `routes.skills.rollback_skill` (alpha gap P1-24): it was a bare\nlookup behind the admin scope alone, which let a global admin who was not a member roll a\nskill back in another project. It now resolves through `_visible_skill_or_404` with the\n`resource.write.runtime` project role.\n</code></pre>\n","status":"passed","flaky":false,"newFailed":false,"newBroken":false,"newPassed":false,"retriesCount":0,"retriesStatusChange":false,"beforeStages":[{"name":"event_loop_policy","time":{"start":1792436381960,"stop":1792436381960,"duration":0},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCount":0,"hasContent":false,"attachmentStep":false},{"name":"monkeypatch","time":{"start":1792436573166,"stop":1792436573166,"duration":0},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCount":0,"hasContent":false,"attachmentStep":false}